---
import { LINKS } from "@/constants/links";
import { ROUTES } from "@/constants/routes";
import { SITE } from "@/constants/site";
import LegalLayout from "@/layouts/legal.astro";
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Refund Policy"
  description={`Cancellations, rescheduling and refunds for ${SITE.NAME} sponsorships.`}
  path={ROUTES.REFUNDS}
  updated="October 2026"
>
  <p>
    The newsletter is free, so this policy covers sponsorship placements bought
    on the <a href={ROUTES.SPONSOR} class="link">sponsor page</a>. There are no
    subscriptions or recurring charges.
  </p>

  <h2>Full refunds</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>We decline your booking during review.</li>
    <li>
      You cancel at least 7 days before your first booked issue goes out.
    </li>
    <li>
      We can't run an issue you booked, or the week was already taken, and you
      don't want to move to another week.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Rescheduling instead of a refund</h2>
  <p>
    If you cancel less than 7 days before a booked issue, we can move you to
    another open week at no cost instead of refunding.
  </p>

  <h2>Bundles</h2>
  <p>
    For a four-issue bundle, issues that haven't gone out yet follow the rules
    above. Issues that already went out aren't refundable; if you cancel the
    rest of a bundle, we refund the unsent issues at the bundle's per-issue
    price.
  </p>

  <h2>After an issue goes out</h2>
  <p>
    A placement that ran as booked isn't refundable. If we made a mistake in
    your sponsor block (wrong link, wrong copy), tell us and we'll fix the issue
    page and either refund or run the corrected block in another issue, your
    choice.
  </p>

  <h2>How to request one</h2>
  <p>
    Email <a href={`mailto:${LINKS.EMAIL}`} class="link">{LINKS.EMAIL}</a> with
    the email you paid with. Refunds go back to the original payment method
    through our payment provider, Dodo Payments, and usually arrive within 5–10
    business days depending on your bank.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
